{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Smith. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You were transferred here from the other hospital because of headaches and back pain. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. Yeah, I’ve had this headache for a few days, and my back’s been bothering me too. Sometimes it’s worse than others. I haven’t been eating much either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:47:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any nausea? Vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:47:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just nausea. No vomiting. I did eat dinner last night, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:48:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. And you mentioned shaking—was that recent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, a few days ago. I thought it might be from my meds. I stopped taking some because of it, but I can’t remember which ones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:50:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. You’re on tacrolimus, which can sometimes cause tremors or confusion. We’ll check your levels and see if that’s playing a role."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I didn’t know that could happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:51:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll run some blood tests today and also check your liver function. Since you’ve had a transplant, we need to make sure everything’s working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:52:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. My wife usually helps me keep track, but she’s not here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-08-15 12:53:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s alright. We’ll piece it together. For now, we’ll start with IV fluids and monitor your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your liver ultrasound came back—good news. The blood flow looks normal, no blockages or masses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about the headache?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Neurology reviewed your prior scans. No stroke or bleeding. But your symptoms are fluctuating, so they want to do an EEG to check for encephalopathy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:18:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Encephalo-what?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:18:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means brain dysfunction, often from toxins or metabolic issues. Given your meds and liver history, it’s something we need to rule out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Could it be the tacrolimus?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:20:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your level was high—13.6. That can cause confusion and tremors. We’re starting to switch you to sirolimus, which is gentler on the brain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll stop tacrolimus?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-08-16 10:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We’ll keep a low dose until your sirolimus level is in range. Then we’ll stop it completely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-08-17 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The EEG was done yesterday. It showed slow brain waves, consistent with encephalopathy. But no seizures. Neurology thinks it’s metabolic or medication-related."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-08-17 14:21:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a stroke?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-08-17 14:21:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. And your strength is symmetric—no signs of stroke. The weakness in your legs is likely from your chronic back issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-08-17 14:22:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that for years. But the confusion—I didn’t expect that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-08-17 14:23:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adjusting your meds to help. Also, your kidney function was a bit off—creatinine was 2.0. It’s improving now to 1.4."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-08-17 14:24:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the meds too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-08-17 14:24:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Tacrolimus can affect kidneys. That’s another reason we’re switching to sirolimus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-08-18 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also found something on your liver imaging—the bile duct near the transplant has a narrowing. It could explain your poor appetite and nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-08-18 09:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-08-18 09:31:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s manageable. You were already scheduled for an ERCP. Since you’re here, we’ll do it tomorrow to open the blockage and place new stents."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-08-18 09:32:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s an ERCP?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-08-18 09:33:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a procedure where a scope goes through your mouth to the bile duct. We’ll remove the old stents, clean out some sludge, and put in new ones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-08-18 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-08-18 09:34:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be sedated, so you won’t feel it. Most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-08-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your ERCP went smoothly. We removed two old stents, cleared out some sludge, and placed three new ones. The duct is now open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-08-19 14:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Will I feel better soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-08-19 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should help your appetite and digestion. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-08-20 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your urine culture back. You have a Pseudomonas infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-08-20 10:06:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-08-20 10:06:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, especially with your health history. But we’ve started nitrofurantoin, which should treat it. You’ll finish the course after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-08-20 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-08-20 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes stomach upset. Take it with food. And drink plenty of water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2179-08-21 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures came back negative—no bloodstream infection. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2179-08-21 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2179-08-22 09:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your mental clarity is improving. The switch from tacrolimus is helping. Your sirolimus level is coming up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2179-08-22 09:41:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel more like myself. Still tired, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2179-08-22 09:41:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. You’ve been through a lot. Physical therapy has been working with you—you’re walking with a walker now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2179-08-22 09:42:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s helping. But I still need help with eating and dressing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2179-08-22 09:43:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s why we’re arranging rehab. You’ll get daily therapy to build strength and independence."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2179-08-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest urine culture showed Enterococcus, but it’s sensitive to the antibiotic. We’ll keep you on nitrofurantoin as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2179-08-23 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same med?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2179-08-23 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and it’s working. Just finish the full course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2179-08-24 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning your discharge tomorrow. You’ll go to a rehab facility for physical therapy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2179-08-24 11:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2179-08-24 11:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be on sirolimus now instead of tacrolimus. We’ll monitor levels closely. Also, lansoprazole for reflux, ursodiol for bile flow, and the antibiotic for five more days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2179-08-24 11:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2179-08-24 11:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, glargine and lispro. We lowered the dose—your glucose was high, but stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2179-08-25 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final update: your labs are stable. Mental status is mostly clear. You’re ready for rehab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2179-08-25 09:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for after I leave?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2179-08-25 09:17:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the transplant team if you get a fever, severe pain, confusion, tremors, or can’t keep food down. Also, get a urine culture next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2179-08-25 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And blood tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2179-08-25 09:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Twice a week. A courier will pick them up. We’ll track your sirolimus and liver numbers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go. The rehab team is expecting you. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just one—will I be able to go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. Rehab will help you regain strength. Most patients return home after a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:02:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:03:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up the good work. We’ll be checking in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Smith."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will help you get ready for transport."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll follow up with your outpatient team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay hydrated and keep eating small meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:08:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Rehab will help even more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the spirit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:11:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll talk soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2179-08-26 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-08-15 12:36:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-08-26 14:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of liver transplant was admitted with headache, back pain, and poor appetite. He had been experiencing confusion and tremors, which were linked to elevated tacrolimus levels. An EEG confirmed encephalopathy likely due to medication toxicity. He underwent an ERCP for a biliary stricture, with successful placement of new stents. A urinary tract infection with Pseudomonas was treated with nitrofurantoin, and his kidney function improved. The patient was transitioned from tacrolimus to sirolimus, and his mental status stabilized. Due to ongoing mobility and self-care challenges, he was discharged to a rehabilitation facility with plans for close outpatient monitoring of medication levels and follow-up urine testing.",
    "problems": [
      "Toxic encephalopathy",
      "Obstruction of bile duct",
      "Complications of transplanted liver",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Diaphragmatic hernia without mention of obstruction or gangrene",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of prostate",
      "Lumbosacral spondylosis without myelopathy"
    ]
  }
}
